<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Porphyra collects, why, and your rights over it."
  lastUpdated="2026-08-07"
>
  <p>
    Porphyra ("we", "us") operates a job-search platform. This policy explains what we
    collect, why, and how it interacts with the end-to-end encryption described on our
    <a href="/security">security page</a>, which takes precedence on any technical detail.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>Content you encrypt yourself</h3>
  <p>
    Your CV, evaluation reports, cover letters, interview notes, contacts, and any job
    description text you paste in are encrypted in your browser before they reach us. We
    store ciphertext. We cannot read this content, and no engineer, support process, or
    legal request to us can produce the plaintext without your password or recovery key —
    see <a href="/security">how the encryption works</a> for the technical detail.
  </p>
  <h3>Structural metadata (not encrypted)</h3>
  <p>
    Application status, dates, the numeric score, ATS vendor, source portal, and your plan
    tier are stored in clear — this is what drives your pipeline view and is not
    individually sensitive. Company and role names are stored as a one-way blind index (see
    the security page), not in clear and not reversible by us.
  </p>
  <h3>Account information</h3>
  <p>
    Email address, authentication data (password hash, not the password itself; 2FA status),
    and billing information if you're on a paid plan (handled by Stripe — we don't store
    card numbers).
  </p>
  <h3>Behavioral analytics</h3>
  <p>
    Feature usage, page views, session length, error rates, and conversion events — never
    the content of what you're evaluating. Web analytics (self-hosted Umami) is cookieless
    and doesn't use persistent identifiers.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the service — evaluating postings, tracking your pipeline, generating documents.</li>
    <li>To bill you, if you're on a paid plan.</li>
    <li>To improve the product — which features get used, where people get stuck.</li>
    <li>To secure the platform — audit logs, abuse and rate-limit detection.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>AI processing</h2>
  <p>
    When you request an evaluation, your CV and the job description are decrypted
    client-side and sent, over TLS, to our AI provider (Anthropic by default) for that one
    request. We do not permit that provider to train on your data, we don't log the request
    body, and the result is re-encrypted before it's stored. This only happens when you take
    the action — never automatically or in the background.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/legal/subprocessors">subprocessors list</a> for every third party that
    touches any part of the pipeline (hosting, email delivery, payment processing, AI
    inference) and what each one can and can't see.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Export your data, correct it, or permanently delete your account and everything in it,
    from account settings at any time. If you're in the EU/EEA/UK, you have rights under
    GDPR (access, rectification, erasure, portability, objection); if you're in California,
    you have rights under the CCPA/CPRA. Email
    <a href="mailto:privacy@porphyra.example">privacy@porphyra.example</a> for anything the
    settings page doesn't cover.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Active account data is kept until you delete it. Deleted-account data is purged from
    primary storage within 30 days and from encrypted backups on their normal rotation
    schedule (documented in full once Phase 6's backup runbook ships).
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis (GDPR)</h2>
  <p>
    Contract performance for providing the service you signed up for; legitimate interest for
    security and product analytics; consent for marketing email (the waitlist, and anything
    opt-in afterward) — withdrawable at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Porphyra is not directed at anyone under 16 and we don't knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>Material changes get emailed to active accounts before they take effect.</p>
</Legal>
